  "verbalization": "Azathioprine, Adenine, and Mercaptopurine share a common ancestry as purines, forming a hierarchical relationship that links them through their structural and functional similarities. This shared purine foundation suggests a potential for overlapping biological mechanisms, particularly in immune modulation and cellular regulation. The evidence indicates that Azathioprine, through its resemblance to Adenine and Mercaptopurine, may influence cellular processes that are implicated in the development of Ulcerative Colitis. The pathway involving Mercaptopurine, which is known to treat Ulcerative Colitis, further supports the notion that Azathioprine could have a similar therapeutic effect. The recurring emphasis on purine-related pathways and the shared treatment effect of Mercaptopurine highlight a possible mechanism by which Azathioprine might contribute to the pathogenesis of Ulcerative Colitis, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
